    "body": "> Review for PR #58073: Prioritize architecture capability before DeepGEMM availability check\r\n> \r\n> ### GPU Capability Hierarchy Analysis\r\n> 1. **Compute Capability Guard Order**:\r\n>    Checking `torch.cuda.get_device_capability() >= (9, 0)` (Hopper/Blackwell architecture) before executing `import deep_gemm` or probing its CUDA symbols prevents misleading dynamic linker (`dlopen`) warnings or aborts on Ampere (sm_80/sm_86) and Ada Lovelace (sm_89) GPUs where DeepGEMM FP8 GEMM instructions are unsupported.\r\n> 2. **Clean Fallback to Standard GEMM**:\r\n>    On pre-sm_90 architectures, the backend cleanly defaults to CUTLASS or Triton FP8 GEMM routines without emitting noisy initialization traceback logs.\r\n\r\nit's not necessarily to be cuda family. I'm considering the logic across all the devices",
